# /etc/resolv.conf — managed by dot (packages/dns). VOID ONLY (runit; no
# systemd-resolved). Installed as a REAL file by configure.sh. This is the resolver
# config that every glibc (files dns) AND musl / c-ares app reads directly, so it
# must always list at least one reachable nameserver. See docs/dns.md.

# --- AdGuard Home (desktop-local resolver, /data/ops/dns) ---
# MUST stay first: it is what gives this box ad/tracker blocking and the local
# *.home.shadhq.com names. It answers on the wildcard :53, so 127.0.0.1 works
# regardless of which interface/network is up.
nameserver 127.0.0.1

# Failover for "AdGuard is down". Deliberately a PUBLIC resolver, not the home
# router (192.168.88.1): this is a laptop-shaped desktop that also sits on foreign
# Wi-Fi, and an unreachable second nameserver costs a full 5 s libc timeout per
# lookup instead of failing over. Quad9 is reachable from any network and matches
# what AdGuard uses upstream (DoH) and what Arch declares as FallbackDNS.
nameserver 9.9.9.9
options edns0
